OL,3,GNEWSAData-breach NHS worker told woman
OL,4,Ashe had cancer
OL,5,
OL,6,FA woman was told she had cancer by a
OL,7,Fhospital employee who accessed her
OL,8,Frecord days before she was due to
OL,9,Freceive test results from her
OL,10,Fconsultant.
OL,12,FPippa Boardman, from Lostwithiel in
OL,13,FCornwall, said she had lost her dignity
OL,14,Fand privacy through the data breach at
OL,15,Fthe Royal Cornwall Hospital in Truro.
OL,16,FShe said she did not receive an apology
OL,17,Ffrom the hospital until it was
OL,18,Fcontacted by the BBC.
OL,20,FThe trust said it was "truly sorry" and
OL,21,F"appropriate action had been taken".
OL,23,APub: 21-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,345,340,200,160,0,100
